<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leeward Islands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Leeward Islands are the northern group of the Lesser Antilles in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, from the Virgin Islands to Dominica. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> settled several of them in the 17th century, and from 1671 the British islands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a>, Nevis, Antigua and Montserrat were governed together as the Leeward Islands colony, later a federation that lasted until 1956.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leeward-islands.jpg" alt="Leeward Islands" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MaligneRange · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:West_Indies_-_Island_Groups.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
